<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN 1996 CAR REGISTRATIONS UP 10.7 PCT IN YEAR.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN 1996 CAR REGISTRATIONS UP 10.7 PCT IN YEAR.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian 1996 car registrations</p>
<p>totalled 397,359 cars, a rise of 10.7 percent over the previous</p>
<p>year, the Belgian automobile industry federation Febiac said in</p>
<p>a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>For 1997 it expected total sales of 385,000 cars, which is</p>
<p>well below the normal replacement rate of 400,000 to 420,000</p>
<p>cars per year.</p>
<p>Febiac also said that registrations for corporate vehicles</p>
<p>such as trucks, vans and buses rose 4.3 percent to 55,382 last</p>
<p>year.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
